Every file in this folder but two is SYNTHETIC: written by hand for these tests
in the shape of each publisher's payload (FRED/ALFRED JSON, BLS v2 JSON, BLS
release schedule pages, BEA NIPA JSON, SEC EDGAR submissions, company facts,
filing indexes, an 8-K's EX-99.1 press release, Form 4/144 XML, 13F
information tables and cover pages, N-PORT documents (each filing's EDGAR index
headers are built from its submissions feed by test_sec.index_headers),
the Federal Reserve's FOMC calendar, statements, Summary of Economic
Projections, minutes and Beige Book pages, FDIC BankFind JSON, the SEC's Money
Market Fund Statistics page (its workbooks are built in tests/data/test_banks.py), NY Fed JSON, Treasury CSV,
FiscalData JSON, Nasdaq calendar JSON, NYSE, SIFMA and OPM holiday pages). The
two exceptions are bls.release_archive__empsit.html and
bls.release_archive__eci.html, trimmed from BLS's public archive pages of
Employment Situation and Employment Cost Index releases (their own list items
and release dates, as each header comment says).

No other file is a recording of a live response. The companies (TESTCO, OTHRCO,
LOSSCO), the managers (CIKs 9999950 and 9999951), the fund (series S000099991,
TFUND), and every CIK, CUSIP, accession number, name, figure and statement in
the SEC filings are invented. The other fixtures are hand-written too, but some
of their values are public ones: FOMC meeting and holiday dates, CPIAUCSL's
first-published values for January and February 2024, and past unemployment
rates (LNS14000000) in the bls.timeseries files. Structured files carry
"_synthetic": true where the format allows it; the SEC ticker lists and the
Treasury CSVs carry none (each keeps the publisher's exact shape) and are
listed here instead: sec.company_tickers.json, sec.company_tickers_mf.json,
fdic.company_tickers.json (sec.company_tickers.json with two invented bank
holders, EXBK and SELF),
treasury.yield_curve__2025.csv and treasury.yield_curve__2026.csv. Page
fixtures say "synthetic" in a comment.

No key appears anywhere: the tests use the obvious fakes in data_harness.KEYS.
